# Chapters 7–8 sensor apps — the application Kconfig.
#
# Two jobs: this product's first real knob (below), and the
# LD2410 log template at the bottom. Per-module log-level symbols
# for our driver exist only where a Kconfig file instantiates
# Zephyr's log-config template for that module name (Chapter 2,
# Step 3) — that is what lets prj.conf aim the driver's log
# level without touching the driver.

menu "Occupancy product behaviour"

config OCCUPANCY_OFF_DELAY_SEC
	int "Seconds of continuous no-presence before the bulb is switched off"
	default 30
	range 0 3600
	help
	  The occupied-to-unoccupied hold time of the product: when
	  the room empties, the bulb stays on for this long before
	  the Off command is sent. Semantically this is the ZCL
	  Occupancy Sensing cluster's UltrasonicOccupiedToUnoccupied-
	  Delay attribute (0x0020); ZBOSS's standard attribute list
	  for the cluster does not declare the delay attributes, so
	  the product implements the same policy in its glue —
	  configurable here, settable per build in prj.conf:
	      CONFIG_OCCUPANCY_OFF_DELAY_SEC=120
	  Zero means "off the moment the room reads empty" — legal,
	  and a fine way to learn why the delay exists.

endmenu

module = LD2410
module-str = HLK-LD2410 driver (Chapters 4 + 7)
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
